<title>USA: Kmart to sell interest in Mexican joint venture.</title>
<headline>Kmart to sell interest in Mexican joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>TROY, Mich. 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kmart Corp. and its Mexican partner said Thursday they will sell their interests in Kmart Mexico SA de CV to a major Mexican retail group, Controladora Comercial Mexicana SA, for $148.5 million in cash.</p>
<p>Kmart and El Puerto de Liverpool SA de CV, each said they will each sell their 50 percent interest in the Kmart Mexico joint venture, which operates three &quot;hypermarket&quot; stores in Mexico City, one in Cuernavaca and will open a fifth store in Puebla this spring.</p>
</text>
